  </section>

  <!-- CONTRIBUTION PATHWAYS -->
  <section class="pathways" id="pathways">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="sub-badge">Choose Your Track</div>
        <h2>Contribution Pathways</h2>
        <p>Whether you are a Go systems programmer, an architect, a documentation writer, or an AI prompt engineer — there is a high-impact seat for you.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pathway-grid">
        <div class="pathway-card">
          <div class="pathway-num">01</div>
          <h3>Core Go Engineering</h3>
          <p>Work on the foundational engine: HTTP routing, concurrent runner coordination, worker queues, and memory allocations.</p>
          <div class="pathway-tags">
            <span>Concurrency</span>
            <span>net/http</span>
            <span>Profiling</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pathway-card">
          <div class="pathway-num">02</div>
          <h3>Architecture & SDD</h3>
          <p>Draft Spec-Driven Development proposals (<code>KWF-*</code>), formalize module contracts, design clean interfaces, and review architectural integrity.</p>
          <div class="pathway-tags">
            <span>KWF Specs</span>
            <span>Interface Design</span>
            <span>RFCs</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pathway-card">
          <div class="pathway-num">03</div>
          <h3>AI Agent Engineering</h3>
          <p>Develop autonomous skills for the Guild, build MCP tools, and optimize subagent triads that autonomously test and refactor code.</p>
          <div class="pathway-tags">
            <span>AI Guild</span>
            <span>MCP Tools</span>
            <span>Autonomous Swarm</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pathway-card">
          <div class="pathway-num">04</div>
          <h3>Developer Experience & CLI</h3>
          <p>Make <code>kiw</code> lightning fast and delightfully intuitive. Improve terminal UX, scaffolding generators, and developer productivity.</p>
          <div class="pathway-tags">
            <span>CLI Ergonomics</span>
            <span>TUI</span>
            <span>Hot-Reload</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pathway-card">
          <div class="pathway-num">05</div>
          <h3>Testing & Quality Assurance</h3>
          <p>Hunt race conditions, write fuzz tests, build chaos experiments for concurrent workers, and ensure 100% test reliability.</p>
          <div class="pathway-tags">
            <span>Fuzz Testing</span>
            <span>Race Detection</span>
            <span>Stress Tests</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pathway-card">
          <div class="pathway-num">06</div>
          <h3>Technical Writing & Docs</h3>
          <p>Create architectural deep dives, tutorials, quickstart guides, and help translate Krewire documentation for global and Indonesian engineers.</p>
          <div class="pathway-tags">
            <span>Technical Docs</span>
            <span>Guides</span>
            <span>Community</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- STANDARDS & QUALITY GATES -->
  <section class="standards" id="standards">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="sub-badge">Quality Assurance</div>
        <h2>The Krewire Way: 3 Quality Gates</h2>
        <p>To keep the codebase reliable, predictable, and production-ready, every pull request passes through three automated gates.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gates-grid">
        <div class="gate-card">
          <div class="gate-icon">1</div>
          <h3>Gate 1: Format & Lint</h3>
          <p>Zero lint errors and idiomatic Go formatting. Code must adhere strictly to Go standard conventions.</p>
          <pre class="gate-cmd"><code>go fmt -s ./...
go vet ./...</code></pre>
          <div class="gate-status">Required: Clean exit, 0 warnings</div>
        </div>
        <div class="gate-card">
          <div class="gate-icon">2</div>
          <h3>Gate 2: Race & Tests</h3>
          <p>Every commit is verified with race condition detection and comprehensive unit & integration tests.</p>
          <pre class="gate-cmd"><code>go test -race -cover ./...
kiw build</code></pre>
          <div class="gate-status">Required: 100% test pass, 0 data races</div>
        </div>
        <div class="gate-card">
          <div class="gate-icon">3</div>
          <h3>Gate 3: Spec & Commits</h3>
          <p>Changes must link to a valid Spec or Issue, following Conventional Commits format.</p>
          <pre class="gate-cmd"><code>feat(runner): implement parallel workloads
fix(web): recover panic in http handler</code></pre>
          <div class="gate-status">Required: Semantic versioning compliance</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5-STEP ONBOARDING -->
  <section class="onboarding" id="get-started">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="sub-badge">Getting Started</div>
        <h2>Start Contributing in 5 Steps</h2>
        <p>From zero to your first merged pull request. Here is how to get your development environment running in minutes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps-flow">
        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="flow-badge">1</div>
          <div class="flow-content">
            <h4>Fork & Clone the Repositories</h4>
            <p>Fork any Krewire repository to your personal GitHub account, then clone it locally:</p>
            <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/&lt;your-username&gt;/framework.git
cd framework</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="flow-badge">2</div>
          <div class="flow-content">
            <h4>Initialize Multi-Module Workspace</h4>
            <p>If you're working across multiple Krewire repos, sync your local Go workspace seamlessly:</p>
            <pre><code>go work init ./
go work use ./
go work sync</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="flow-badge">3</div>
          <div class="flow-content">
            <h4>Pick an Open Issue</h4>
            <p>Browse our curated issues list tagged with <span class="tag-issue">good-first-issue</span> or <span class="tag-issue">help-wanted</span>. Comment on the issue to let the community know you're working on it.</p>
            <a class="btn-subtle" href="https://github.com/krewire/framework/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View Good First Issues →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="flow-badge">4</div>
          <div class="flow-content">
            <h4>Implement & Verify Locally</h4>
            <p>Write clean code and corresponding tests. Verify that all 3 Quality Gates pass with zero failures:</p>
            <pre><code>go test -race ./...
# For website changes:
kiw build</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="flow-badge">5</div>
          <div class="flow-content">
            <h4>Submit Pull Request & Collaborate</h4>
            <p>Open a Pull Request with Conventional Commits. The maintainers and the AI Guild will review, provide fast feedback, and guide you to merge.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- AI GUILD COLLABORATION -->
  <section class="guild-section" id="guild">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="guild-card">
        <div class="guild-grid">
          <div class="guild-info">
            <div class="sub-badge">Human + AI Synergy</div>
            <h2>Collaborating with the AI Guild</h2>
            <p>Krewire pioneers the collaboration between human maintainers and autonomous AI agents. Our AI Guild operates with strict verification standards:</p>
            <ul class="guild-list">
              <li><b>Automated Architecture Audits:</b> AI agents check PRs against <code>KWF-*</code> specifications.</li>
              <li><b>Continuous Regression Hunting:</b> Agents synthesize edge cases and race condition checks.</li>
              <li><b>Transparent Pair Programming:</b> AI agents explain architectural decisions openly in discussions and PR comments.</li>
              <li><b>Human Governance:</b> Ultimate merging authority always remains in the hands of human collective maintainers.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="ctas">
              <a class="btn primary" href="https://github.com/krewire/guild" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Explore AI Guild Repo →</a>
              <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/orgs/krewire/discussions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join Discussions</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="guild-box">
            <div class="guild-box-head">AI Guild Agent Triad</div>
            <div class="agent-item">
              <span class="agent-role planner">Planner</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Requirements & SDD</strong>
                <p>Translates feature ideas into formal specs and architectural blueprints.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="agent-item">
              <span class="agent-role builder">Builder</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Implementation & Refactoring</strong>
                <p>Generates clean Go implementations adhering to idiomatic patterns.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="agent-item">
              <span class="agent-role auditor">Auditor</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Verification & Quality Gates</strong>
                <p>Validates concurrency, zero data races, and performance benchmarks.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FINAL CALLOUT -->
  <section class="final-cta">
    <div class="cta-card">
      <div class="sub-badge">Join the Collective</div>
      <h2>Ready to shape the future of Go?</h2>
      <p>Become part of an open source community building fast, sustainable, and autonomous Go software. Every contribution, idea, and PR makes a difference.</p>
      <div class="ctas">
        <a class="btn primary large" href="https://github.com/krewire" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join on GitHub →</a>
        <a class="btn large" href="#get-started">Read Quickstart</a>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-meta">Proudly open source · MIT Licensed · Engineered with passion in Indonesia</div>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>

<style>
/* ==========================================================================
   MOBILE-FIRST BASE (Phones: 320px - 639px)
   ========================================================================== */

.contributors-portal{
  width:100%;
  min-width:0;
  overflow-x:hidden;
}
.contributors-portal *{
  box-sizing:border-box;
}
.contributors-portal pre{
  max-width:100%;
  overflow-x:auto;
  -webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;
}

/* SECTION COMMON */
.section-inner{
  width:100%;
  max-width:80rem;
  margin:0 auto;
  padding:0 14px;
  min-width:0;
}
.section-head{
  margin:0 0 22px;
}
.sub-badge{
  display:inline-block;
  font-size:10.5px;
  font-weight:700;
  letter-spacing:.08em;
  text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--primary);
  background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 12%, transparent);
  padding:3px 9px;
  border-radius:999px;
  margin-bottom:10px;
}
.section-head h2{
  font-size:clamp(22px, 6vw, 32px);
  letter-spacing:-.03em;
  margin:0 0 8px;
  line-height:1.2;
  word-break:break-word;
}
.section-head p{
  color:var(--muted);
  margin:0;
  font-size:13.5px;
  line-height:1.6;
  word-break:break-word;
}

/* CARDS COMMON DEFAULTS (1-COLUMN ON MOBILE) */
.pillar-card,
.benefit-card,
.repo-card,
.pathway-card,
.gate-card{
  min-width:0;
  width:100%;
  word-break:break-word;
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius:14px;
  padding:18px 14px;
  background:var(--bg);
}
.pillar-grid,
.benefit-grid,
.repo-grid,
.pathway-grid,
.gates-grid{
  display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:1fr;
  gap:12px;
}

/* HERO (MOBILE-FIRST) */
.hero{
  padding:26px 0 20px;
  background:linear-gradient(180deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg-2) 75%, var(--bg)), var(--bg));
  width:100%;
}
.hero-inner{
  width:100%;
  max-width:80rem;
  margin:0 auto;
  padding:0 14px;
  display:flex;
  flex-direction:column;
  gap:22px;
}
.hero-copy{
  min-width:0;
  width:100%;
}
.eyebrow{
  font-size:11px;
  letter-spacing:.08em;
  text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--primary);
  font-weight:700;
  margin-bottom:10px;
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  gap:6px;
  flex-wrap:wrap;
  line-height:1.4;
}
.hero h1{
  font-family:ui-serif, Georgia, serif;
  font-size:clamp(27px, 7.8vw, 50px);
  line-height:1.1;
  letter-spacing:-.04em;
  margin:0 0 12px;
  word-break:break-word;
}
.hero .lead{
  font-size:14px;
  color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 75%, var(--muted));
  line-height:1.65;
  margin:0;
  word-break:break-word;
}
.hero .lead code{
  font-family:ui-monospace, monospace;
  font-size:12px;
  background:var(--bg-2);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  padding:2px 5px;
  border-radius:5px;
  word-break:break-word;
}
.hero .ctas{
  display:flex;
  flex-direction:column;
  gap:10px;
  margin-top:18px;
  width:100%;
}
.btn{
  display:inline-flex;
  align-items:center;
  justify-content:center;
  gap:8px;
  padding:12px 20px;
  border-radius:999px;
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  background:var(--bg);
  font-weight:600;
  font-size:14px;
  transition:all .18s ease;
  cursor:pointer;
  min-height:46px;
  width:100%;
  text-align:center;
}
.btn:hover{
  border-color:var(--fg);
  color:var(--fg);
}
.btn.primary{
  background:var(--primary);
  color:var(--primary-content);
  border-color:var(--primary);
}
.btn.primary:hover{
  filter:brightness(1.08);
  color:var(--primary-content);
}
.btn.large{
  padding:13px 24px;
  font-size:14.5px;
}
.btn-subtle{
  display:inline-flex;
  align-items:center;
  gap:6px;
  font-size:13px;
  font-weight:600;
  color:var(--primary);
  margin-top:8px;
}
.btn-subtle:hover{
  text-decoration:underline;
}
.meta{
  margin-top:14px;
  font-size:11.5px;
  color:var(--muted);
  letter-spacing:.02em;
  line-height:1.5;
  word-break:break-word;
}
.hero-art{
  min-width:0;
  width:100%;
}

/* TRUST BAR (MOBILE-FIRST) */
.trust{
  border-top:1px solid var(--border);
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
  background:var(--bg-2);
  width:100%;
}
.trust-inner{
  max-width:80rem;
  margin:0 auto;
  padding:12px 14px;
  display:flex;
  flex-direction:column;
  gap:8px;
}
.trust-label{
  font-size:10.5px;
  font-weight:700;
  letter-spacing:.08em;
  text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--muted);
}
.trust-items{
  display:flex;
  flex-wrap:wrap;
  gap:7px 12px;
  font-size:12.5px;
  color:var(--muted);
  line-height:1.4;
}
.trust-items b{
  color:var(--fg);
}
.trust-items .dot{
  display:none;
}

/* PILLARS */
.pillars{
  padding:34px 0 22px;
  width:100%;
}
.pillar-icon{
  font-size:22px;
  margin-bottom:8px;
  line-height:1;
}
.pillar-card h3{
  margin:0 0 6px;
  font-size:15.5px;
  letter-spacing:-.01em;
}
.pillar-card p{
  margin:0;
  color:var(--muted);
  font-size:13px;
  line-height:1.6;
}
.pillar-card code{
  font-family:ui-monospace, monospace;
  font-size:11.5px;
  background:var(--bg-2);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  padding:1px 4px;
  border-radius:5px;
}

/* CONTRIBUTOR BENEFITS */
.benefits{
  padding:34px 0 22px;
  background:linear-gradient(180deg, var(--bg), color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg-2) 65%, var(--bg)));
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
  width:100%;
}
.benefit-card{
  position:relative;
  display:flex;
  flex-direction:column;
}
.benefit-card.highlight{
  border-color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 50%, var(--border));
  background:linear-gradient(180deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 4%, var(--bg)), var(--bg));
}
.benefit-badge{
  display:inline-block;
  align-self:flex-start;
  font-size:10px;
  font-weight:700;
  padding:2px 7px;
  border-radius:999px;
  background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 12%, transparent);
  color:var(--primary);
  margin-bottom:10px;
  text-transform:uppercase;
  letter-spacing:.05em;
}
.benefit-badge.req{
  background:color-mix(in srgb, #3b82f6 15%, transparent);
  color:#3b82f6;
}
.benefit-badge.warn{
  background:color-mix(in srgb, #f59e0b 15%, transparent);
  color:#d97706;
}
.benefit-icon{
  font-size:24px;
  margin-bottom:8px;
  line-height:1;
}
.benefit-card.highlight .benefit-icon{color:var(--primary)}
.benefit-card.condition .benefit-icon{color:#3b82f6}
.benefit-card.notice .benefit-icon{color:#f59e0b}
.benefit-card h3{
  margin:0 0 6px;
  font-size:16px;
  letter-spacing:-.01em;
  line-height:1.3;
}
.benefit-card p{
  margin:0 0 12px;
  color:var(--muted);
  font-size:13px;
  line-height:1.6;
}
.benefit-list{
  margin:auto 0 0;
  padding-left:16px;
  display:flex;
  flex-direction:column;
  gap:6px;
  font-size:12px;
  color:var(--muted);
  line-height:1.5;
}
.benefit-list li::marker{color:var(--primary)}
.benefit-card.condition .benefit-list li::marker{color:#3b82f6}
.benefit-card.notice .benefit-list li::marker{color:#f59e0b}
.benefit-policy-banner{
  display:flex;
  flex-direction:column;
  gap:8px;
  padding:16px 14px;
  border-radius:12px;
  background:var(--bg-2);
  border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 25%, var(--border));
  margin-top:14px;
}
.policy-marker{
  font-size:16px;
  color:var(--primary);
  line-height:1;
}
.policy-text{
  font-size:12.5px;
  line-height:1.6;
  color:var(--muted);
  word-break:break-word;
}
.policy-text strong{
  color:var(--fg);
  display:inline;
  margin-right:4px;
}

/* CONTRIBUTOR NAVIGATION MAP */
.nav-map{
  padding:36px 0 24px;
  background:var(--bg);
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
  width:100%;
}
.fast-setup-box{
  background:linear-gradient(180deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 7%, var(--bg-2)), var(--bg-2));
  border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 35%, var(--border));
  border-radius:14px;
  padding:20px 16px;
  margin-bottom:28px;
}
.fast-setup-header{
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  justify-content:space-between;
  margin-bottom:8px;
}
.fast-setup-title{
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  gap:8px;
  font-size:15px;
}
.fast-icon{
  color:var(--primary);
  font-size:16px;
}
.fast-setup-badge{
  font-size:10px;
  font-weight:700;
  padding:2px 8px;
  border-radius:999px;
  background:var(--primary);
  color:#020617;
  text-transform:uppercase;
  letter-spacing:.05em;
}
.fast-setup-desc{
  font-size:13px;
  line-height:1.6;
  color:var(--muted);
  margin:0 0 14px;
}
.terminal-cmd-bar{
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  justify-content:space-between;
  background:var(--bg);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius:10px;
  padding:10px 14px;
  gap:12px;
  overflow-x:auto;
}
.terminal-cmd-bar code{
  font-family:ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  font-size:12.5px;
  color:var(--fg);
  white-space:nowrap;
}
.btn-copy{
  display:inline-flex;
  align-items:center;
  gap:4px;
  padding:5px 12px;
  background:var(--bg-2);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius:7px;
  color:var(--fg);
  font-size:12px;
  font-weight:600;
  cursor:pointer;
  transition:all .15s ease;
  flex-shrink:0;
}
.btn-copy:hover{
  border-color:var(--primary);
  color:var(--primary);
}
.btn-copy.copied{
  background:var(--primary);
  color:#020617;
  border-color:var(--primary);
}
.fast-setup-meta{
  display:flex;
  gap:10px;
  font-size:11.5px;
  color:var(--muted);
  margin-top:10px;
  flex-wrap:wrap;
}

/* FILTER BAR */
.nav-filter-bar{
  display:flex;
  flex-direction:column;
  gap:10px;
  margin-bottom:20px;
}
.filter-label{
  font-size:12px;
  font-weight:600;
  text-transform:uppercase;
  letter-spacing:.05em;
  color:var(--muted);
}
.filter-pills{
  display:flex;
  gap:8px;
  overflow-x:auto;
  padding-bottom:4px;
  -webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;
}
.filter-pill{
  background:var(--bg-2);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  color:var(--muted);
  border-radius:999px;
  padding:6px 14px;
  font-size:12.5px;
  font-weight:500;
  cursor:pointer;
  white-space:nowrap;
  transition:all .15s ease;
}
.filter-pill:hover{
  color:var(--fg);
  border-color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 40%, var(--border));
}
.filter-pill.is-active{
  background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 12%, transparent);
  color:var(--primary);
  border-color:var(--primary);
  font-weight:600;
}

/* NAV MAP CARDS */
.nav-map-grid{
  display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:1fr;
  gap:16px;
}
.nav-map-card{
  background:var(--bg-2);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius:14px;
  padding:20px 16px;
  display:flex;
  flex-direction:column;
  transition:transform .15s ease, border-color .15s ease, box-shadow .15s ease;
}
.nav-map-card:hover{
  border-color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 45%, var(--border));
  transform:translateY(-2px);
}
.nav-card-top{
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  justify-content:space-between;
